WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
The funniest part of my job

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.150
on a day when JB Smoove is coming in,

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:07.680
is inevitably someone,

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.410
today it was Aaron Bleyaert,
sitting right over there,

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.213
texting to try and get a
reservation at a fast food chain.

00:00:15.213 --> 00:00:18.510
(audience laughs)

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:21.307
I love that you walked
in, Bley, and you're like,

00:00:21.307 --> 00:00:22.830
"Here's some possible notes

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.920
of what you could talk
about with JB Smoove."

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.910
And I always, there is no more
ridiculous thing in the world

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:31.830
than for someone to
spend time writing down

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.110
things I might talk to JB about,

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:37.380
because I never have any idea
what we're gonna talk about.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.230
I never have, you can't plan any of that.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.330
You shouldn't plan any of that.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.640
I never know what's gonna
happen and it just happens.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:45.720
I don't know about you guys,

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.840
but I don't know, some,
talking to JB, there's a,

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.820
a moment or two where my, where my mind

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.380
wandered just a little bit, I think,

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:53.213
when he was talking about

00:00:53.213 --> 00:00:54.780
some of the crazier stuff he wanted to do.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:55.680
What were you thinking about?

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.060
I was thinking about EVs.

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:58.251
That's my term for-

00:00:58.251 --> 00:00:59.180
I was too. That's weird.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.462
Yeah, I was thinking
about electric vehicles.

00:01:00.462 --> 00:01:01.740
That's cool.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.410
Yeah, just because I
keep thinking, you know,

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.150
it used to be kind of weird.

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:07.530
This person has an electric vehicle.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:08.550
Isn't that kind of strange?

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.110
But now EVs are everywhere.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:11.640
And you know who's killing it with EVs?

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:12.539
Who?

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:13.830
One guess?

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:14.663
Yeah. One guess.

00:01:14.663 --> 00:01:15.496
Chevy.

00:01:15.496 --> 00:01:17.550
Yes. Chevy.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.285
That was very natural.

00:01:19.285 --> 00:01:21.870
Man, incredible. Yeah.
Chevy's killing it with EVs.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:22.770
Yeah.

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.510
They've got one for everybody.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:25.770
Anyway, I was thinking about

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:28.170
all the different types
of Chevys they have.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:33.170
Chevy EVs. And you can buy
the Bolt EV or the Bolt EUV.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.493
Wow.

00:01:34.493 --> 00:01:37.950
Reserve the Blazer EV or the Silverado EV.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.270
Yeah. That's your favorite.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.052
[Conan] I love the Silverado
just 'cause of the name.

00:01:41.052 --> 00:01:41.885
Yeah.

00:01:41.885 --> 00:01:44.580
Yeah. I just walked into
a bar, and you're a lady

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:47.220
sitting at the bar, and you
saw me pull up in a truck.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.110
Ask me what kind of truck I drive.

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:51.060
Hey, what kind of truck do you drive?

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.563
Silverado.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:54.360
And I leave.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:55.193
[Conan] You leave.

00:01:55.193 --> 00:01:56.026
Yeah.

00:01:56.026 --> 00:01:56.991
But I'm still here.

00:01:56.991 --> 00:01:57.824
Not because you have
anything against Silverado,

00:01:57.824 --> 00:01:59.400
but because you think that I
have something wrong with my-

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.470
It's because you said
it really weird. Yeah.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.780
Yeah. No, Silverado EV. And learn more

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.020
about the Equinox EV

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:08.820
while staying tuned for
more info on Chevy's vision

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.250
for an electronic future.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:12.120
Electric.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:12.953
What's it?

00:02:12.953 --> 00:02:14.160
It's an electric future.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.290
Oh. And I said that you
would screw up the card.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:19.050
Do we get the check if
I keep f@*#ing around?

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:19.883
We lost the check minutes ago.

00:02:19.883 --> 00:02:20.716
We have to pay Chevy.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.150
Yeah. We owe them.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:27.191
No one has ever paid
us for any of our ads.

00:02:27.191 --> 00:02:28.024
(everyone laughs)

00:02:28.024 --> 00:02:30.420
To learn more about the Chevy EV lineup,

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:34.563
head to chevrolet.com/conan. Yeah.

